		orig := nodeString(fset, lit)
		// orig is like `func(x int) int { return fn(x) }` – need exact? Our nodeString may give `func(x int) int {\n\treturn fn(x)\n}` with newline? But original message shows single line `func(x int) int { return fn(x) }`.
